---
import Footer from "./Footer.astro";
const skillGroups = [
  {
    title: "Programming",
    intro:
      "My study focuses on mathematical problems, mainly in AI, Machine Learning, and Signal/Image Processing. I also read lots of documentation about AI automation, computer systems, CI/CD workflows, and system optimization. Sometimes I do math for 3D modelling or animated visualizations (just for fun, btw).",
    rows: [
      { label: "Languages", items: ["C/C++", "Python", "Java", "TypeScript", "Bash"] },
      { label: "Databases", items: ["MySQL/MariaDB", "MongoDB", "ChromaDB"] },
      {
        label: "Machine Learning & AI",
        items: [
          "Scikit-Learn",
          "PyTorch",
          "TensorFlow",
          "Keras",
          "OpenCV",
          "Transformers",
          "Diffusers",
          "LangChain"
        ]
      },
      {
        label: "Backend & Web",
        items: ["Spring Boot", "Quarkus", "Maven", "React", "REST", "gRPC"]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    title: "Tech Stacks",
    rows: [
      { label: "Development & Operations", items: ["Git", "Docker", "Kubernetes", "Datadog"] },
      { label: "Data & Storage", items: ["Supabase", "Qdrant"] },
      { label: "Cloud Platforms", items: ["AWS", "GCP", "MS Azure"] },
      { label: "Virtualization", items: ["RHEV", "OpenStack", "VMware ESXi"] }
    ]
  },
  {
    title: "Fundamental Knowledge",
    rows: [
      { label: "Computer Science", items: ["Algorithms", "OOP", "Kernel & System", "Networking"] },
      {
        label: "AI & Data",
        items: ["Machine Learning", "Deep Learning", "Feature Learning/Engineering", "RAG", "OCR"]
      },
      { label: "Signal Processing", items: ["Digital Signal/Image Processing"] },
      {
        label: "Engineering Practices",
        items: ["CI/CD Workflows", "Vector Database/Embedding/Search"]
      }
    ]
  }
];
---

<section id="more" class="section more" data-planet-panel="earth">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section__heading" data-reveal="@heading">
      <span class="section__num" data-reveal-part="num">
        03.
      </span>{" "}
      <span class="section__title" data-reveal-split>
        More About Me
      </span>
    </h2>

    <div class="more__grid">
      <article
        data-resize-flip
        class="more__card more__card--wide surface-card"
        data-reveal="@card"
        data-spotlight
      >
        <h3 class="more__title">Why I chose Computer Science</h3>
        <p>
          Working with numbers is my cup of tea. I really like natural sciences, especially Math,
          Physics, and Chemistry (but not good enough to win any awards 🙃). It is just very
          interesting and enjoyable to answer the question "why is it like that?", and I love
          discussing everyday natural phenomena with others.
        </p>
        <p>
          I started programming in high school, with C++ as my first language. Back then I only
          learned how to solve basic algorithm problems. Now it's not only about the solution but
          also the optimization, which is definitely the hardest part :)
        </p>
      </article>

      <div class="more__group more__card--wide">
        <h3 class="more__group-title" data-reveal="@eyebrow">
          My Skills
        </h3>
        <div class="more__skills" data-resize-flip-group>
          {skillGroups.map((group) => (
            <article
              data-resize-flip
              class="more__card surface-card"
              data-reveal="@card"
              data-spotlight
            >
              <h4 class="more__title more__title--sm">{group.title}</h4>
              {group.intro && <p>{group.intro}</p>}
              <dl class="more__rows">
                {group.rows.map((row) => (
                  <div class="more__row" data-reveal="@chip" data-reveal-items="dt, li">
                    <dt>{row.label}</dt>
                    <dd>
                      <ul class="more__chips">
                        {row.items.map((item) => (
                          <li class="surface-chip">{item}</li>
                        ))}
                      </ul>
                    </dd>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </dl>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <article data-resize-flip class="more__card surface-card" data-reveal="@card" data-spotlight>
        <h3 class="more__title">Operating System</h3>
        <p>
          Linux is my main operating system for most of my work. I started with Fedora in high
          school. Now I use Arch Linux "by the way", plus popular Red Hat distros (RHEL, Oracle
          Linux, CentOS) at work. For my homelab and self-hosted servers I pick the most lightweight
          and stable distro: Debian.
        </p>
        <p>
          I use Windows only for… playing games… and MS Visual Studio, which only supports Windows
          due to its reliance on DLLs, so… 🤕
        </p>
      </article>

      <article data-resize-flip class="more__card surface-card" data-reveal="@card" data-spotlight>
        <h3 class="more__title">Free time only for studying???</h3>
        <p>
          I'm not that crazy about studying, even in my free time. I play some "wjbu" games such as
          Genshin Impact and Honkai: Star Rail, and I read books, manga, or daily tech news whenever
          my phone is in my hand. I also played FPS games like CS2 on Steam and Valorant (very
          rarely now).
        </p>
        <p>
          Terraria and Oxygen Not Included are two "offline" games I really spent time on, and I
          highly recommend both survival and adventure games. Ping me for anything gaming!
        </p>
        <a
          class="btn btn--ghost more__cta"
          href="mailto:3dbrogaming2003@gmail.com"
          data-reveal="@button"
        >
          Talk games with me
        </a>
      </article>

      <article
        data-resize-flip
        class="more__card more__card--wide more__card--solar surface-card"
        data-reveal="@card"
        data-spotlight
      >
        <span
          class="more__accent"
          aria-hidden="true"
          data-reveal="@line"
          data-reveal-delay="200"
        ></span>
        <h3 class="more__title">The Solar System? …</h3>
        <p>
          Why the Solar System? … Remember the question "why it is?" I like so much? Space is full
          of them :D How do the planets keep orbiting? Why does Saturn have rings? It is the same
          fun I get from Math and Physics, so when I was thinking about how to decorate this site, a
          small solar system came to mind right away.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each planet keeps a part of this site, just click one and fly there. Doing the math for
          the orbits, the lighting, and the camera was really fun, btw (and a bit painful at some
          points 🙃).
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
  <Footer panel />
</section>

<style>
  .section__heading {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    min-width: 0;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .section__title {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .more__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .more__card--wide {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .more__card {
    min-width: 0;
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur);
    border: var(--glass-border);
    border-radius: var(--card-radius);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .more__card p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .more__card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .more__title {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: var(--text-title);
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .more__title--sm {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .more__group-title {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .more__skills {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .more__rows {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .more__row dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-label);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .more__chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    list-style: none;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .more__chips li {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-chip);
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--color-text);
    background: var(--glass-bg-subtle);
    border: var(--glass-border-subtle);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .more__cta {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  /* The card's 1px left border stays transparent; the 2px accent rule sits
     on the padding edge just inside it (absolute offsets are measured from
     the padding box, so the bar cannot overlay the border slot). Hover and
     planet hover repaint every border side, so the left edge is re-pinned
     to transparent with selectors that out-rank both. */
  .more__card--solar {
    position: relative;
    border-left-color: transparent;
    overflow: clip;
  }

  html .more__card--solar:hover,
  html .more__card--solar:focus-visible,
  html main [data-planet-theme] .more__card--solar:hover,
  html main [data-planet-theme] .more__card--solar:focus-visible {
    border-left-color: transparent;
  }

  .more__accent {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 2px;
    background: rgba(255, 204, 51, 0.55);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .more__skills {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (orientation: portrait), (max-width: 720px) {
    .more__grid,
    .more__skills {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  /* Phones: tighter spacing and type so cards stay compact and readable */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .section__heading {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    }

    .more__grid {
      gap: var(--space-sm);
    }

    .more__group {
      margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    }

    .more__card {
      padding: clamp(0.9rem, 4vw, 1.1rem) clamp(0.8rem, 4vw, 1rem);
    }

    .more__card p {
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .more__title {
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .more__title--sm {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .more__rows {
      gap: 0.7rem;
    }

    .more__cta {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      width: 100%;
    }
  }

  /* Very small phones (≈320px) */
  @media (max-width: 360px) {
    .more__card {
      padding: 1rem 0.85rem;
    }
  }
</style>
